{"id": "EUVD-2026-93283", "enisaUuid": "44932679-22c4-3760-8492-7881987993e7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndmaengine: mmp_pdma: fix wrong sg length in mmp_pdma_prep_slave_sg()\n\nIn mmp_pdma_prep_slave_sg(), for_each_sg() iterates the scatterlist\nputting each entry into 'sg', but the entry length is read from 'sgl'\n(the list head) instead of 'sg' (the current entry):\n\n    for_each_sg(sgl, sg, sg_len, i) {\n        addr = sg_dma_address(sg);\n        avail = sg_dma_len(sgl);   /* should be 'sg' */\n\nConsequently 'avail' is always the length of the first entry. For\nmulti-sg lists this causes out-of-bounds reads when a later entry is\nshorter than the first, and silent data loss when it is longer.\nSingle-sg or uniformly-sized lists happen to mask the issue.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f448a5f5bd10d792440a1b08cf2e8f311767032d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2148db529f082d6e3ca95413bf943442f4ef30cc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d920c07aa6d89ec11afdb6976aafaee9563a5234", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4a33886057e6d127555efb022879c583e966acc5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88a505330eb06128f7ce79a4c5e4832b7601b3d1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bae65e4925928f77824ca0103122e2ed20ef5802", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/54ccc01012a240476edf641bf1a2b8bff54fe6ae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/075bc7b1d3dde5ed43fbaabbc1a69f09b7fc3a47"], "aliases": ["GHSA-262v-749m-59x9", "CVE-2026-98298"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "10c39917-0b18-3207-b859-b7a2c4e1981a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c8acd6aa6bed3c0fd7898202f4ebc534db9085f2 <d920c07aa6d89ec11afdb6976aafaee9563a5234"}, {"id": "204ddd12-9126-3808-a2f9-cbff28426e14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "2967d4cc-8054-3751-8f10-a251373fd18f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.7"}, {"id": "39fe4a35-58f4-3180-a10e-31cccd0faa65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c8acd6aa6bed3c0fd7898202f4ebc534db9085f2 <f448a5f5bd10d792440a1b08cf2e8f311767032d"}, {"id": "44ff0358-afa9-37e8-8bb4-8fefe1e2d572", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c8acd6aa6bed3c0fd7898202f4ebc534db9085f2 <54ccc01012a240476edf641bf1a2b8bff54fe6ae"}, {"id": "69959eb8-46a2-3390-b4d4-4b731a7d55f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "6de2f073-5a84-3045-b6c9-7d9b1f6d1aa7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "72b95957-d25b-3a52-b031-b43d04731760", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "7513570f-f57b-37cd-879e-47654491843c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c8acd6aa6bed3c0fd7898202f4ebc534db9085f2 <88a505330eb06128f7ce79a4c5e4832b7601b3d1"}, {"id": "7e7308dc-a95b-3c7b-bec3-8d36748ec593", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c8acd6aa6bed3c0fd7898202f4ebc534db9085f2 <4a33886057e6d127555efb022879c583e966acc5"}, {"id": "831559f9-75df-3349-b495-a5ccec412bc4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "8c826820-ae77-35a6-9e33-e7751c115884", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "9d5ec4b5-e576-390f-9365-3bab5a8d2c33", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c8acd6aa6bed3c0fd7898202f4ebc534db9085f2 <bae65e4925928f77824ca0103122e2ed20ef5802"}, {"id": "b3646221-519b-3668-9f8e-b83b0a93f8a7", "product": {"name": "Li